            <ArticleTitle>[Recurrent corneal erosion. Apropos of a case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>358-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recurrent corneal erosion (RCE) is a disease which often occurs in women. The authors report one case of RCE in the right eye of a 38 year old woman age. Clinical signs and clinical course under treatment are described. The pathogenesis and treatment of RCE are also described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
